{"title":"National Internet Math Olympiad","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>National Internet Math Olympiad (NIMO)</b> was a team-based series of online math tests for high school students. It was organized by Evan Chen.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Contests\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Contests</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Online_Math_Open\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Online Math Open</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#NIMO_Summer_Contest\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">NIMO Summer Contest</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#NIMO_Monthly_Contest\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">NIMO Monthly Contest</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Contests\">Contests</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=National_Internet_Math_Olympiad&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Contests\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Online_Math_Open\">Online Math Open</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=National_Internet_Math_Olympiad&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Online Math Open\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <b>Online Math Open (OMO)</b> was a math Olympiad held in fall and spring. There are 30 questions (each worth 1 point), and each answer is a nonnegative integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e2b7f43a232abba3461db4d35a06c73f8a74810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{31} - 1 = 2147483647$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"169\" height=\"15\" />. The test lasts for 12 days. The only electronic math tool allowed is a four-function calculator.\n</p>\n<table style=\"border:thin solid black;padding:10px;float:right;margin:10px;background:#fff;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"border:thin solid gray;text-align:center;background:#ccf;\"><b>OMO</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Region</b>: USA\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Type</b>: Short Answer\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS_Wiki:Competition_ratings\" title=\"AoPS Wiki:Competition ratings\">Difficulty</a></b>: 1-9.5\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Difficulty Breakdown:</b>\n<p><u>Problem 1-5</u>: 1-3<br /><u>Problem 6-10</u>: 3-4 <br /><u>Problem 11-15</u>: 4.5-5.5 <br /><u>Problem 16-20</u>: 6 <br /><u>Problem 21-25</u>: 7-8 <br /><u>Problem 26-30</u>: 8-9.5\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"NIMO_Summer_Contest\">NIMO Summer Contest</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=National_Internet_Math_Olympiad&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: NIMO Summer Contest\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <b>NIMO Summer Contest</b> was another online contest where each question was worth the respective question’s number points. Solvers can not return to a problem when a problem was skipped.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"NIMO_Monthly_Contest\">NIMO Monthly Contest</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=National_Internet_Math_Olympiad&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: NIMO Monthly Contest\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <b>NIMO Monthly Contest</b> has 8 questions that must be solved in 40 minutes. Solvers can submit up to 3 attempts.\n</p><p>As of 2018, the NIMO Monthly Contest has been discontinued.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=National_Internet_Math_Olympiad&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewforum.php?f=581\">AoPS Forum</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018101014\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 39/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 496/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 198/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 193/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.477      1 Template:Contest_Info\n100.00%    7.477      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16729:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018101014 and revision id 238347. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}